Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:15:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11134/11362] [outer-loop] Parse the flag ledger instead of
 pattern-matching it (REQ-INFRA-6840)

Recording a measured null made the flag invisible. --record-null writes an
evidence block above the entry's state line. flag_states captured the text
from a flag's name to the next bare 'key:' and searched that window for
'state:', and 'evidence:' is itself a bare key, so the window closed early.
Both flags returned '?' and fell out of BOTH categories: the headline read
2/4 shipped-but-untested, 0 measured-null while the ledger held two
off_measured entries.

The bug was latent and I exposed it an hour ago by recording the nulls the
operator authorized. The more evidence a flag carried, the more certainly it
disappeared from the dashboard.

Now reads the document. An unknown flag, an unreadable ledger or a malformed
one reports '?', never 'unevaluated': a wrong 'unevaluated' is an answer and
invents a coverage gap, while '?' is a question. Two of the three mutations
cover that clause alone.

Rejected: widening the regex to skip 'evidence:'. That fixes this key and
leaves the class, and the next writer to add a nested block underneath a flag
reintroduces it.

Also records, without fixing, a limitation of the attention line shipped
earlier tonight: it counts the day's escalation rows and cannot know an
escalation was resolved, because the log records no resolution. Read it as
'raised today', not 'open now'.

5 tests, 3/3 mutations RED with byte-identical restores; M1 reverts to the
exact regex and reproduces the incident.

